Task: reject <, <=, >, >= against null in the protodb/v2 filter parser.

Changes: parser.go guards the four ordering operators with isNullConst and returns an error that Parse wraps as ErrInvalidFilter; filter_test.go adds TestNullInOrderingComparisonIsInvalid (null on either side).

Files: protodb/v2/filtering/parser.go, protodb/v2/filtering/filter_test.go

Why: an ordering comparison with NULL is never true in Spanner, so silently emitting SQL hid a caller mistake.
